# 🟢 Part 4: Display Linked List

To see what’s inside the list:

```c
void displayList() {
    if (head == NULL) {
        printf("List is empty.\n");
        return;
    }
    struct Node* temp = head;
    printf("Linked List: ");
    while (temp != NULL) {
        printf("%d -> ", temp->data);
        temp = temp->next;
    }
    printf("NULL\n");
}
```

### 🔎 Explanation:
- Start from head.
- Traverse using `temp = temp->next`.
- Print until `NULL` is reached.

